# Generic timed capture: no menus, no X tools. Wait for the game process, let it settle,
# record a fixed stretch between two markers, then quit. Useful for:
#  - games with a command-line benchmark mode (add the flag with args= in the experiment)
#  - idle/attract scenes or a fixed spot you load into automatically
#  - consistent fixed-length captures of anything
# Experiment:  hook=gamerun-uiflow ~/.config/gamerun/flows/timed-capture.flow
#              bench_window=markers:capture_start:capture_end
# Edit the process name and timings for your game.

set on_fail "MyGame"
process "MyGame" 300        # regex on the process name (Proton games: the .exe name, e.g. Game\.exe)
sleep 60                  # loading, shader compilation, settling
mark capture_start
sleep 120                 # the measured stretch
mark capture_end
quit "MyGame"
